WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:02.460
You have other guests?

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:06.140
Yes. They arrived just the two before you.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.190
Now, please have a seat.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.650
Thank you.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:14.280
What's wrong, you three?

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.400
Aren't you going to come and sit down?

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.770
What? Anne!

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.290
Huh? What?

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:22.810
For fairies to eat in front of people 
is completely absurd!

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.560
Why? We usually eat together, don't we?

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.480
What?

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.160
No, but this is in front of other people!

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.760
During our travels, 
we have all been eating together.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:36.040
Would it be possible to do the same here?

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.870
Well...

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:40.260
I am not the type to mind...

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.840
But, you know, there are other guests here.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.270
It doesn't bother us! Pay me no mind.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.160
Hey there, young miss. What's your name?

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.030
It's Anne. Anne Halford.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.030
I'm Hugh. There's no need to 
stand on formalities, Anne.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.200
Do as you like.

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:29.210
I see.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:33.610
So, you're on this road 
because you're heading for Lewiston.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:38.670
The Sugar Confectionary Exhibition is being 
held in Lewiston, and we're planning to enter!

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:42.120
Really? So, you're both sugar artisans?

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.340
If that's the case...

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:46.280
having two labor fairies 
and one companion fairy is a little...

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:47.600
extravagant, I'd say.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.650
Challe isn't a companion fairy, 
he's a warrior fairy!

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:51.770
He's my guard!

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.360
Warrior fairy? You're such a liar.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.690
I'm not lying!

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.700
Now, now. There's no need 
to feel embarrassed.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.280
A fairy who looks like that... 
Of course you'd want to bring him with you.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.790
Anne, did you fall for that fairy? 
Is that why you bought him?

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:06.990
It isn't like that!

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:09.700
Then, shall we put it to the test?

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.050
Challe!

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:18.710
Not bad.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:21.130
Do you want to be killed?

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.590
Unfortunately, I'm not quite that broken.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:26.080
That's enough, Salim. Withdraw your sword.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.700
What do you think you're doing, 
you absolute idiot!

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:31.690
If you harm my companions, 
you will not get away with it!

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.400
Sorry about that.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:37.130
I just can't believe that such a pretty, 
high-quality warrior fairy exists.

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:39.130
Is that any reason to do something like this?

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.550
I said I'm sorry, didn't I?

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:42.640
Let's see...

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.450
As an apology, I'll pay for your stay here.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:46.910
Don't try to brush past this like—

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:49.290
Pay... for our stay?

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.370
Yes. For all five of you.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.890
Though, I feel like I'll be 
taking a loss if I do that.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:59.160
I know! How about you two make 
some sugar confections for me?

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.210
What?

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.460
Ones the size of a fist will do.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.430
That'll take care of 
the cost of your stay here.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.460
Not a bad deal, right?

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:07.850
All right.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.140
In exchange, you make sure 
you pay for our stay.

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:14.100
Jonas, will you pull out two bowls for me?

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.800
Oh, of course.

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:16.810
Thanks.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.030
Is it all right to use that silver sugar?

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:23.630
You still have to make your 
piece for the exhibition, don't you?

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:26.240
Yes, but I have more than enough.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.200
I can't use what's in those 
three barrels, though.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:32.360
So, that's what you'll be 
submitting to the exhibition.

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:35.420
Well, they do also assess entrants' 
sugar-refining skills, don't they?

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.980
I'm starting to feel excited.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:41.320
Getting to unveil my skills in front of 
people makes me feel so proud!

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:42.740
Does it?

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:43.300
There.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.480
Actually, just between us,

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:49.660
I might be recommended to become 
the head of the school I belong to!

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.610
The master of the Radcliffe Workshop school?

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:52.390
Yes.

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:54.640
Of course, to become the master,

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:58.540
I have to be awarded a royal medal 
and become a silver sugar master.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:04:59.110
Um...

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:02.820
Then, why don't you enter 
the exhibition this time, too, Jonas?

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:06.800
No, this time I'll just watch.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:09.410
But, for the sake of my future, 
I <i>have</i> to become one!

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:13.290
If I don't, then I can't become 
the master or the Silver Sugar Viscount!

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:15.880
The Silver Sugar Viscount?

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.720
You mean the silver sugar master 
who works exclusively for the royal family?

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.630
Jonas, you want to become someone like that?

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.110
Of course I do!

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:24.090
Or rather, I will definitely become that!

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.320
I mean, for a commoner like me 
to be able to become a noble...

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:30.160
There isn't any dream 
more wonderful than that, is there?

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:31.290
Which is why, Anne...

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.500
won't please you marry me?

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.520
I'll become the Silver Sugar Viscount,

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.480
and make your life a happy—

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.440
Jonas.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:42.020
I'm sorry.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.760
Let's not talk about that anymore.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:49.920
I've readied all the equipment for you.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:52.480
There's no need to color 
the sugar confections.

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:54.660
And I'll leave the form to the two of you.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.480
Who are you, exactly?

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:59.630
Could it be that you're a sugar artisan, too?

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:04.090
If you want me to pay for your stay here, 
then just keep quiet and make something, Anne.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:09.680
<i>What should I make?</i>

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:11.640
<i>If it were Mama,</i>

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:14.620
<i>she'd make the most of 
the silver sugar's natural color.</i>

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.360
Both of you are quite proficient.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:28.040
Neither of you seem like novices.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:30.020
However...

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:34.020
What have you done?!

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:37.160
They were unsightly, so I destroyed them.

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:39.210
Jonas.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:41.920
You're skilled, but that's all.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.320
All you want to do 
is show off your technique,

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:45.880
so you haven't added any 
of your own ingenuity of all.

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:48.730
Anne, you did better than Jonas.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:51.090
But what was this?

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:56.060
It's as though you created this in imitation 
of something someone else had made.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.350
You're simply aping their style.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:01.120
It was pretty, but that's all. 
It had no charm to it.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.120
With work like this,

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:06.420
your dreams of becoming a silver sugar 
master are no more than dreams.

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:11.490
But I will accept these 
sugar confection fragments.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:13.850
I'll have them as a snack.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:17.580
Bye, then, Anne. Jonas.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:20.120
That was a nice way to kill time. It was fun!

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:25.850
What was that man trying 
to accomplish with that?

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:28.260
Master Jonas! 
There is no need to let it bother you!

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:31.600
That's right, Anne! A man like that is—

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:32.550
Hey, Anne!

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.850
Hold on, Anne!

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:35.510
Anne, come on!

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.140
A bagworm again?

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:43.600
What is so funny?

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:46.060
Is it really so amusing to see 
someone depressed?!

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:50.380
What? Why would you look 
at someone's face and laugh?

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:54.620
Well, a scarecrow like me will only be an 
embarrassment no matter what I do anyway!

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:58.620
Humans never spend their
 whole lives being laughed at.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.900
For, unlike us, they are always changing.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.310
You will, in another three years...

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.510
have become startlingly beautiful.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:16.090
The color of your hair 
will turn a pale, beautiful gold...

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:20.020
and your skill at making sugar 
confections will change, too.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:24.490
I will hone my skills in making 
sugar confections even more.

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:26.810
I'll show him how much I can improve!

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:31.660
But there are some things that 
can't be changed with hard work.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:34.070
I don't need transparent lies to comfort me.

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:35.830
They aren't lies.

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:37.700
I know.

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:43.210
When I was born, the first thing 
I saw was a human child...

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:45.960
One with hair the same color as yours...

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:47.460
A five-year-old girl.

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:52.630
I was born because of that child's gaze.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.230
That girl was Liz...

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.970
Her name was Elizabeth.

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:01.950
Liz was the daughter of nobles...

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:04.780
and because of certain circumstances, 
she lived away from society.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:07.930
She was young, knew nothing of the world,

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:10.180
and didn't know of the existence of fairies.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:15.240
That's why she mistook me 
for her own older brother.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:19.660
She led me back to her 
mansion and gave me shelter.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:22.840
Fifteen years passed.

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:25.370
Liz's hair turned a pale gold...

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:26.990
her freckles disappeared...

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:28.700
and she became a beautiful young woman.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:30.670
That's why I know.

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:33.590
You will continue to change, just as Liz did.

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:36.510
What happened? What happened to Liz?

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:40.220
Did she stay with you always? 
Why isn't she here now?

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.100
She died.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:46.750
She was killed.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:48.520
Humans killed her.

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:53.320
I'm sorry.

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:58.520
Go to sleep, Scarecrow.

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:09.880
That Hugh person paid for our stay 
just as he promised he would.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:11.420
Hey, Anne!

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:12.520
Are you listening?

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:20.340
<i>Challe said he wouldn't be 
friends with a human.</i>

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:25.400
<i>But in the beginning, 
he had an emotional bond with a human girl.</i>

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:30.560
<i>He spent the same amount of time
 with her that I had with Mama.</i>

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:35.560
<i>For Challe, Liz might have been like family.</i>

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:39.320
<i>And that was stolen from him by human hands.</i>

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:43.530
<i>Humans caused Challe's heart to freeze over.</i>

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:48.120
It's cold tonight, isn't it?

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:51.960
We do not feel the cold as humans do.

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:59.880
<i>I wish there was magic 
that could melt Challe's heart.</i>

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:05.320
<i>The promise I made to Challe...</i>

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:08.140
<i>the sugar confection I promised him... 
I'll make it now.</i>

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:10.770
<i>A sweet sugar confection...</i>

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:15.150
<i>I hope it can bring even 
a little warmth to Challe's heart.</i>

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:26.460
Wh-Why...

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:30.520
The silver sugar... is gone?

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:34.130
It can't be. Why is it gone?

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:35.900
What's happened?

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:39.920
The silver sugar is gone.

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:41.300
Gone?

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.230
I have three barrels left.

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:46.510
But I don't have any silver sugar 
to use in making my entry piece.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:49.390
Anne? Has something happened?

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:51.210
Anne!

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:59.030
Apparently, the silver sugar she needs 
to make her piece has disappeared.

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:02.960
What? But the silver sugar 
was in the cargo hold, wasn't it?

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:04.380
And it was locked!

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:06.530
No one could get in or out, could they?

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:08.960
No, it was possible to gain entry.

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:10.750
What do you mean by that, Cathy?

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:14.650
I saw it. That night when 
we stayed at the doctor's inn.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:18.710
Mithril Lid Pod came out of the window 
of Mistress Anne's cargo hold!

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:21.920
In the moonlight, his whole body sparkled.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:24.060
That was him all covered in silver sugar!

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:25.870
Mithril?

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:27.930
What's all this?

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.740
You sure are being loud.

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:31.480
Mithril. Come down here.

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:35.260
Hey! I don't serve you!

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:37.150
And don't shorten my name!

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:37.610
I am—

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:39.160
Come down here!

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:40.650
Wh-What is it?

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:43.400
Anne's silver sugar has disappeared.

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:46.220
Mithril, you stole it, didn't you?

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:46.870
What?

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:49.100
Cathy saw you.

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:51.330
Saw me? Sh-She's lying!

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:54.440
Hey, Anne. I wasn't the one who stole it.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:55.790
Cathy's the liar here!

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:58.540
What would Cathy gain by lying?

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.570
Blasted human, be quiet!

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:04.250
Anne, you aren't suspicious 
of me, too, are you?

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:07.130
It wasn't me. I swear to you, it wasn't me!

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:08.360
I...

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:10.790
Anne...

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:13.480
You do suspect me.

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:16.280
You don't believe me, do you, Anne?

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:18.190
I want to believe you.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:20.400
But you <i>don't</i>, do you?!

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:23.480
Fine, then. If you're going to 
look at me like that, then...

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:25.450
I'll just disappear from your sight, Anne!

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:26.110
Mithril!

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:27.120
Wait!

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:36.120
I can't participate in 
this year's exhibition like this.

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:39.880
I know, Anne!

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:42.440
If you only need enough for one piece,

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:45.300
then all you need to do 
is make that much silver sugar!

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:49.360
That's unrealistic. I don't have the
 sugar apples needed to make it.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:50.600
Don't worry!

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:51.260
What?

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:53.720
There are sugar apples!

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:57.980
I heard about it at a gathering 
of the Radcliffe Workshop school.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:01.680
They say that there's a grove of 
sugar apple trees on the Bloody Highway!

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:04.300
It takes three days to refine silver sugar.

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:07.840
But if you use the silver sugar 
you already have for your piece,

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:09.360
you'll be able to make it in time!

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:16.340
Sugar apples!

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:19.710
There are five days 
left until the exhibition.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:23.410
Lewiston isn't far from the next fortshelter.

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:24.850
With these...

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:26.670
It will be all right, Anne.

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:30.890
I'm a bit of a sugar artisan, 
too. I'll help you.

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.890
Thank you, Jonas! Let's get started!

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:06.970
Here.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.860
Where is Mithril?

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:11.360
Disappeared.

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:13.090
Where has he gone?

00:15:13.670 --> 00:15:17.980
Was it really him? 
Was it really Mithril who stole it?

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:19.530
I don't know.

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:22.440
The truth is, I don't care 
who stole the silver sugar.

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:26.380
In any case, I will make sure 
my work is finished in time.

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:27.280
I told you, didn't I?

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:30.790
I absolutely <i>must</i> enter 
this year's exhibition.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:33.240
I'll go back to work.

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:38.240
<i>The piece I am submitting 
for the exhibition...</i>

00:15:38.650 --> 00:15:40.710
<i>will be a sugar confection 
for a celebration...</i>

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:43.920
<i>large, bright, and beautiful.</i>

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:46.760
<i>Mama...</i>

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:50.380
This is the wealth Mama has made.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:52.720
It can't be given to anyone,

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.740
and it mustn't be imitated.

00:15:57.830 --> 00:16:02.360
<i>It's as though you created this in imitation 
of something someone else had made.</i>

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:03.560
<i>You're simply aping their style.</i>

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:07.990
<i>Then, what should I make? And how?</i>

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:10.260
<i>I just don't know.</i>

00:16:16.480 --> 00:16:19.870
If you'd like, please use this barrel 
to put your silver sugar in!

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:22.840
It's a first-rate article 
that guards against humidity.

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:25.440
But I already have two empty barrels.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:28.170
Wow! So, you've decided 
what you're going to make?

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:31.420
Anne, you really are amazing. I can tell.

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:33.790
I'm certain that you'll be able 
to create a wonderful piece!

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:35.390
I hope so, but...

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:37.370
I expect a lot of you.

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:38.100
What?

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:39.640
Wh-What are you doing?

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:42.110
I love you.

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:42.890
Don't!

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:46.910
Why, Anne?

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:49.360
Jonas, I don't love you!

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:51.190
But I love you!

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:54.820
That's how you feel, Jonas! 
It isn't how I feel!

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:57.160
I see.

00:16:57.970 --> 00:17:01.480
I had hoped that you would 
fall in love with me, but...

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:04.040
I-I'm sorry. I...

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:06.780
I'm sorry, Anne.

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:12.880
Mistress Anne, I will give you 
one piece of advice.

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:14.840
What is this, all of a sudden?

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:18.440
Master Jonas might propose to you, 
or say he loves you,

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:20.100
but don't let it go to your head!

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:20.890
What?

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:25.360
Master Jonas would never actually 
fall in love with someone like you!

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:26.410
Cathy...

00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:27.480
Could it be that you...

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:30.040
Are you in love with Jonas?

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:31.080
Th...

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:32.640
Th-Th-Th...

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:34.880
That's completely absurd!

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:37.210
I see! So that's what's going on!

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:40.680
It's so lovely when fairies 
and humans get together, isn't it?

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:43.410
Y-You are...

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:46.250
such an idiot!

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:51.160
<i>The person Cathy is in love 
with is holding her wing.</i>

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:52.840
<i>Compared to that...</i>

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:57.880
<i>Love between a fairy and a human.</i>

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:01.260
<i>I wonder what was between Challe and Liz.</i>

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:05.350
<i>What's this? My chest feels tight.</i>

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:09.350
It's something that has 
nothing to do with me.

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:13.120
<i>The reason Challe is with me...</i>

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:15.880
<i>is because I hold his wing.</i>

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:19.590
<i>And when we reach Lewiston, 
that will end too.</i>

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:24.970
It's done!

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:29.960
<i>It should be perfect, and yet...</i>

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:32.960
You're simply aping their style.

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:36.700
<i>No. The technique is perfect.</i>

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:37.860
<i>It will be all right.</i>

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:40.680
<i>I'm sure it will be all right!</i>

00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:44.680
Have you finished?

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:46.360
It's drying now.

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:49.070
I'll grind what's left of 
the silver sugar using the mortar,

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:50.810
and if we set out tomorrow,

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:54.100
we'll be able to make it to Lewiston 
the day before the exhibition.

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:55.820
It was strange.

00:18:57.390 --> 00:19:00.430
When I first met you at the fairy market,

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:02.540
you smelled of the sweetness of silver sugar.

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:05.950
I couldn't understand why. It was strange.

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:09.640
Do I? I wonder if the scent 
has seeped into my dress.

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:11.470
Your fingers.

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:12.170
What?

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:15.780
Your fingers carry a sweet scent.

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:17.960
No, they don't.

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:19.180
I can tell.

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:20.220
Really?

00:19:26.030 --> 00:19:27.260
I see.

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:30.350
Anne!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:32.730
Anne! You're amazing, Anne!

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.840
You finished your piece!

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:38.270
I've never seen such a large 
piece as delicate as that!

00:19:38.270 --> 00:19:40.410
You'll get the royal medal, and no mistake!

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:41.630
Thank you!

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:44.780
This is all possible because you told me 
about the sugar apples, Jonas!

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:47.240
I'm the one who should be thanking you!

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:51.720
What are you doing at my wagon, Jonas?

00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:53.630
I thought we should set off.

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:58.460
You're being too hasty. 
The silver sugar isn't done yet.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:00.880
And that horse isn't mine...

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:05.800
It's not a problem! 
My horse runs faster than yours.

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:07.540
Jonas?

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:12.320
If you'd fallen in love 
with me and married me,

00:20:12.320 --> 00:20:14.250
then I wouldn't have had 
to do something like this.

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:15.440
It's all your fault.

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:16.650
What are you trying to do?

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.610
This is why I told you 
not to let it go to your head!

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:22.990
Ow! What?

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:23.660
What is this?

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:26.070
It's disgusting!

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:34.440
Challe, what is all this?

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:35.830
Those two lured them here...

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.720
so that they could steal 
your sugar confection.

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:40.040
That can't be!

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:41.550
Bye-bye, Anne!

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:44.220
Challe, go after Jonas!

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:47.100
If I leave this spot, 
you will become food for the wolves!

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:49.950
That doesn't matter! Please, go!

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:51.660
Challe! I'm begging you!

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:53.470
Please bring my sugar confection back!

00:20:53.470 --> 00:20:54.230
I refuse!

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:56.190
Please! Challe!

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:58.940
Please bring my sugar confection back!

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:04.950
The Sugar Apple Is the Tree of Betrayal

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:40.000
<b>The Fate of the Royal Medal</b>
